  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Higher Education Capacity Development (HECD) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  The Higher Education Capacity.Development (HECD) activity will increase capacity in higher education institutions.(universities, colleges, and institutes) to better prepare their graduates with.the necessary work-based learning and job readiness skills to respond to the.demands of the Lebanese, regional, and global labor markets. Through this.activity, USAID will provide professional development and support to nine.higher education institutions (HEIs) to improve their institutional capacity to.transfer and train their students with in-demand technical and soft skills as.they enter the labor market. In addition, HECD will strengthen HEI internal.systems to effectively support student career resource centers and enhance.student employability prospects. Using FY 2022 resources, around 4,000 students.will benefit from practical and activity-based job skills training programs,.making them more attractive to employers and better prepared to enter the.workforce, which in turn contribute to Lebanon&apos;s economic recovery and growth..This activity is attributed to the higher education earmark..</narrative>
  </description>
